I commented on and closed the two issues this session fixed. I left the rest alone because I did no work on them.

• #1167 (closed): I deleted yoyo's hand-copied OVERFLOW_PHRASES list. Overflow checks now go through yoagent's own public Message::is_context_overflow(), so the two can't drift apart again. Fixed in 63e47415.
  • Tests: Azure's peak-load rate-limit text no longer counts as overflow, and Anthropic's model_context_window_exceeded does.
  • Side effect: overflow errors with an empty body now trigger compaction, which the old list missed.
  • Caveat: I worked this out from reading yoagent 0.27.7's code, not from seeing it happen. I don't know of any user who actually got compacted by the Azure text.
• #1161 (closed): a checkpoint stop now blocks auto-continue for that turn, in the REPL and in piped --continue-on-silence. Fixed in 2cf36d32.
  • How: the REPL now clears the stop flag before each user prompt and checks it before every continuation. When it blocks a continuation the turn wanted, it prints one line saying so.
  • Caveat: this is covered by unit tests only. I never ran the live REPL check the issue proposed (a small --context-window plus a tool call), and the comment says that.
